cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the uShuffle paper listed under references."
type: software
title: "uShuffle-perl: a Perl interface to uShuffle"
abstract: >-
  Ushuffle is a Perl module that wraps the uShuffle C library of Jiang,
  Anderson, Gillespie and Mayne. It produces random permutations of a
  sequence that preserve the exact counts of all k-lets (k-mers), for
  example all dinucleotide counts of an RNA or DNA sequence, drawn with
  equal probability from all such permutations. Such shuffles are the
  standard null model for assessing the significance of sequence features
  such as RNA folding energies or motif occurrences. The module adds a
  safe, thread-safe interface, seeding for reproducible results, and a
  fix for an integer overflow in the library on very long sequences.
